# 4. ORDER ITEMS DATA QUALITY VALIDATION

# Table: bronze.olist_order_items

# ====================================================================

## Business Objective

Order item validation ensures accurate revenue,
shipping, and product-level sales analysis.

---

## 4.1 Check NULL Values

### Purpose

Detects incomplete transactional records.

```sql
SELECT
    SUM(CASE WHEN order_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS order_id_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN order_item_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS order_item_id_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN product_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS product_id_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN seller_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS seller_id_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN shipping_limit_date IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS shipping_limit_date_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN price IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS price_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN freight_value IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS freight_value_nulls
FROM bronze.olist_order_items;
```

---

## 4.2 Check Duplicate Order Items

### Purpose

Ensures uniqueness of order item combinations.

### Expected Result

No rows returned

```sql
SELECT
    order_id,
    order_item_id,
    COUNT(*) AS duplicate_count
FROM bronze.olist_order_items
GROUP BY
    order_id,
    order_item_id
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;
```

---

## 4.3 Detect Negative Monetary Values

### Purpose

Validates pricing integrity.

### Expected Result

No rows returned

```sql
SELECT *
FROM bronze.olist_order_items
WHERE price < 0
   OR freight_value < 0;
```

---

## 4.4 Detect Zero Price Orders

### Purpose

Identifies potential promotional, test,
or corrupted transactions.

```sql
SELECT *
FROM bronze.olist_order_items
WHERE price = 0;
```

---

