# 5. ORDER PAYMENTS DATA QUALITY VALIDATION

# Table: bronze.olist_order_payments

# ====================================================================

## Business Objective

Payment data validation ensures accurate financial reporting
and payment method analysis.

---

## 5.1 Check NULL Values

```sql
SELECT
    SUM(CASE WHEN order_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS order_id_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN payment_sequential IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS payment_sequential_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN payment_type IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS payment_type_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN payment_installments IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS payment_installments_nulls,
    SUM(CASE WHEN payment_value IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS payment_value_nulls
FROM bronze.olist_order_payments;
```

---

## 5.2 Check Duplicate Payments

### Purpose

Ensures payment sequence uniqueness.

```sql
SELECT
    order_id,
    payment_sequential,
    COUNT(*) AS duplicate_count
FROM bronze.olist_order_payments
GROUP BY
    order_id,
    payment_sequential
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;
```

---

## 5.3 Validate Payment Types

### Purpose

Review payment method standardization.

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT payment_type
FROM bronze.olist_order_payments
ORDER BY payment_type;
```

---

## 5.4 Detect Negative Payment Values

### Purpose

Ensures financial values remain valid.

```sql
SELECT *
FROM bronze.olist_order_payments
WHERE payment_value < 0;
```

---

## 5.5 Validate Installment Values

### Purpose

Installment counts should always be positive.

```sql
SELECT *
FROM bronze.olist_order_payments
WHERE payment_installments <= 0;
```

---

## 5.6 Analyze Undefined Payment Types

### Purpose

Measures unknown or unclassified payment records.

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) AS not_defined_count
FROM bronze.olist_order_payments
WHERE payment_type = 'not_defined';
```

