# 8. SILVER LAYER DERIVED METRIC VALIDATION

# Table: silver.olist_orders

# ====================================================================

## Business Objective

The Silver layer introduces derived analytical metrics
used for logistics and SLA performance analysis.

---

## 8.1 approval_time_hours

### Formula

```sql
DATEDIFF(HOUR, order_purchase_timestamp, order_approved_at)
```

### Business Meaning

Measures how quickly orders are approved after purchase.

### Analytical Use Cases

* Seller operational efficiency
* Order processing bottlenecks
* Internal workflow analysis

---

## 8.2 delivery_days

### Formula

```sql
DATEDIFF(DAY, order_purchase_timestamp, order_delivered_customer_date)
```

### Business Meaning

Measures total customer delivery time.

### Analytical Use Cases

* Delivery performance
* Logistics optimization
* Customer experience analysis

---

## 8.3 estimated_delivery_days

### Formula

```sql
DATEDIFF(DAY, order_purchase_timestamp, order_estimated_delivery_date)
```

### Business Meaning

Represents promised delivery timeline communicated to customers.

### Analytical Use Cases

* SLA analysis
* Promise vs actual comparison
* Delivery expectation management

---

## 8.4 is_delayed

### Formula

```sql
CASE
    WHEN order_delivered_customer_date > order_estimated_delivery_date THEN 1
    ELSE 0
END
```

### Business Meaning

Indicates whether delivery exceeded the promised delivery date.

### Analytical Use Cases

* SLA breach analysis
* Delay tracking
* Logistics KPI monitoring

